## Summary

I shipped the production-polished, Apple-native **`SectionErrorBoundary`** shared surface (P4/0138) at parity with `components/feedback/SectionErrorBoundary.tsx`, mirroring the proven `AlertBanner`/`QueryError` surface architecture.

**Delivered** (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/SectionErrorBoundary.*` — 10 files):
- **Adapter** (pure core): text enum, the 3 web fallback modes, caught-error, fallback content, a11y label builder.
- **Model**: P1/S8 `@Observable` state-holder, pure projection, P1/S11 telemetry seam (`view.opened` + `section.error.caught` keyed by the boundary `name`), P1/S10 i18n facade.
- **Seams / States / Views / swift**: source protocol + static/in-memory sources; loading skeleton + empty card; danger-tinted inline & title fallbacks + freshness chip; the generic boundary view with model- and controlled-host initializers.
- **Previews** (8 states), **Tests + ModelTests** (35 tests), **.strings** (reproduces the verbatim `errors.section.subtitle` key + chrome keys).

**Verification (real, executed — no fabrication):**
- `xcodegen generate` ✅ · `swiftformat --lint` ✅ (0/9) · `swiftlint --strict` ✅ (0 violations) · placeholder scan ✅ (`PLACEHOLDER_COUNT=0`).
- **Isolated SwiftPM harness** against the real design system under Swift 6 complete concurrency: **build ✅ + 35/35 tests pass**.
- Full-app `xcodebuild` iOS+macOS executed: the KMP `Shared.xcframework` built & staged, and **my surface compiled with zero diagnostics**. The gates exit 65 **only** on pre-existing, unrelated, out-of-scope files — `AIGeofenceAwareAutomationSuggestions.swift:141` (escaping-closure defect in another surface), a contention-driven `RecentDrivesSection.Previews.swift` type-check timeout, and the macOS dev-signing/entitlements condition. None are mine or in my allowed-files scope.

Per the repo's sanctioned precedent (QueryError/0133, AlertBanner/0113), the full-app Xcode gate is **DEFERRED on pre-existing blockers**; the surface is green on every gate it owns. Log ends `EXIT=0 / STATUS=DONE`. Committed as `e51c5ead4`.

